-- Should type-check, but the checker fails with
--   Error: in file Implicit_lambda_capture.batt line 15 characters 6-7, term has type Unit but bool expected
--
-- When a clause is checked against a type whose head is an implicit Π, here {u : ⊤} → bool
-- (after unfolding P), the checker inserts an implicit lambda and names its variable after the
-- binder of the type, u. That inserted variable then shadows the clause variable u, so the u in
-- the body is the implicit argument (of type ⊤) instead of the explicit one (of type bool).
-- Inserted variables should not be in scope by name. Renaming the clause variable (f b = b) makes
-- the definition check, and so does f ∷ (u : bool) → {u : ⊤} → bool with the binder written inline.

P ∷ U → U
P X = {u : ⊤} → X

f ∷ (u : bool) → P bool
f u = u
